From d54e7fdd01684ba2eeb402e501bf7f10e43eee3b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dgabehar <dgabehar@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:09:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] FLEET: correct the 2026-11-10 sync's wrong grammar-regression
 attribution

test_speculative.py::test_grammar_drafts_unless_no_spec_grammar's write-up blamed
src/llama-grammar.cpp (zero fork code, zero conflicts) and upstream's 48c9f08b7
grammar-candidate-rejection rewrite. That was never verified, and is wrong:
checking out llama-grammar.cpp + its header from pre-merge-2026-11-10 onto the
post-merge tree still reproduces the exact same divergence. common/sampling.cpp
(the fork's grammar-first/resample drafting logic) also has zero diff across
the merge, ruling out the fork's own drafting path too.

Root-caused instead to Vulkan's NVIDIA coopmat1 matmul path specifically:
CPU never reproduces it; GGML_VK_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 (Intel iGPU) passes, =1
(NVIDIA RTX 3080 Ti Mobile) fails; on NVIDIA, GGML_VK_DISABLE_COOPMAT=1 alone
fixes it, GGML_VK_DISABLE_COOPMAT2=1 alone does not. Also ruled out: the fork's
own flop-based Vulkan submit-batching (forcing flops_per_submit=0 still fails)
and the KQ attention matmul's explicit precision request in build_attn_mha
(d6be06557's F32->BF16 change has no effect -- both map to the same
ggml_vk_prec_allows_f16acc()==false result). 459a1ba54's small-matmul-tile
rederivation is also ruled out: its formula reduces to the exact same tile
value on a 32-wide-subgroup device, which this NVIDIA GPU is (the commit
targets 8/16-wide Mali/mobile subgroups). Likeliest remaining, unpinned
candidate: 8e5a58df8 ("vulkan: ggml src1 precision support", #30656), which
reworked coopmat1 accumulator-precision/kernel selection across many matmuls.

This is the same already-documented near-tied-logit/batch-size-numerics
category this file's "Known-fragile areas" already names for the
SSM_CONV_SPLIT/qwen3-coder case, not a new logic bug in the grammar engine or
the drafting path. No fleet impact: production runs AMD UMA nodes only, no
NVIDIA, so it was reported and documented rather than mitigated (no coopmat1
disable, no revert of 8e5a58df8, which also fixes real production fp16-overflow
bugs). Not fixed upstream: only 4 trivial commits exist past 202c1a229, none
touching llama-grammar.cpp, ggml-vulkan/, or llama-graph.cpp.

Full tools/server/tests -m "not slow" rerun (clean venv, openai+jiter
importable) reconfirms baseline exactly: 483 passed, 5 skipped, 2 failed
(test_n_probs_post_backend_sampling, test_grammar_drafts_unless_no_spec_grammar)
-- no new regressions from this correction.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet
