+- **`--spec-grammar` is not bit-exact on near-tied logits on NVIDIA's Vulkan coopmat1 path (found 2026-11-10,
+  not fixed, no fleet impact known).** `tools/server/tests` `test_speculative.py::test_grammar_drafts_unless_no_spec_grammar`
+  fails deterministically on this workstation's Vulkan build (`GGML_VULKAN=ON GGML_RPC=ON`, NVIDIA RTX 3080 Ti Mobile +
+  Intel UHD 770 iGPU) since the 2026-11-10 upstream sync (`202c1a229`): with `--spec-grammar` on, the greedy
+  completion under `grammar: "root ::= [a-z]+ (\" \" [a-z]+)*"` diverges from plain (no-draft) greedy decode at token
+  index 1 (`322` vs `297` in one capture) -- both outputs stay grammar-valid, only the token sequence differs.
+  Repro: `GGML_VK_VISIBLE_DEVICES=1 LLAMA_SERVER_BIN_PATH=<path>/llama-server python3 -m pytest
+  unit/test_speculative.py::test_grammar_drafts_unless_no_spec_grammar -x` from `tools/server/tests`, with a Vulkan
+  build (CPU-only never reproduces it).
+  - **Ruled out (verified, not hypothesis):** `src/llama-grammar.cpp`/`.h` (checked out from `pre-merge-2026-11-10`
+    onto the post-merge tree, still fails identically); `common/sampling.cpp`/`.h` (zero diff across the merge); the
+    fork's own flop-based Vulkan submit-batching/graph-splitting in `ggml_vk_graph_compute`, `ggml-vulkan.cpp` (forced
+    `flops_per_submit = 0`, still fails -- not a scheduling/sync bug in the fork's own merge-conflict resolution); the
+    KQ attention matmul's explicit accumulation-precision request in `src/llama-graph.cpp`'s `build_attn_mha`
+    (upstream `d6be06557` changed it `GGML_PREC_F32` -> `GGML_PREC_BF16`; reverting that one line back to F32 has no
+    effect, and reading `ggml_vk_prec_allows_f16acc()` in `ggml-vulkan.cpp` shows F32 and BF16 both map to
+    `return false` there, so the two values are equivalent for this path); and `459a1ba54`'s small-matmul-tile
+    rederivation specifically (`s_warptile_wm_8 = 32 * subgroup_size_8 / subgroup_size_32` reduces to the old
+    `device->subgroup_size == 8 ? 8 : 32` formula's value exactly on a 32-wide-subgroup device, which the NVIDIA GPU
+    here is -- the commit targets Mali/mobile 8/16-wide subgroups, not NVIDIA).
+  - **Isolated (verified):** `GGML_VK_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0` (Intel UHD iGPU) passes; `=1` (NVIDIA) fails. On the NVIDIA
+    device, `GGML_VK_DISABLE_COOPMAT=1` alone makes it pass; `GGML_VK_DISABLE_COOPMAT2=1` alone does not. So the cause
+    is specifically in the `VK_KHR_cooperative_matrix` (coopmat1) matmul path on NVIDIA, not coopmat2, not a generic
+    GPU-vs-CPU numeric difference, and not the fork's own code anywhere in the merge's conflict resolutions.
+  - **Not pinned down further (reported, not verified):** which exact upstream commit inside the coopmat1 path is
+    responsible was not isolated past the point above -- the likeliest remaining candidate in the merge's commit set
+    is `8e5a58df8` ("vulkan: ggml src1 precision support", #30656), which reworked the coopmat1
+    accumulator-precision/kernel-selection logic (`ggml_vk_get_mul_mat_mat_f16acc` and friends) for *many* matmuls
+    throughout the graph, not just KQ; `70c5f2632` ("vulkan: rms norm optimization using subgroup reductions", #29882)
+    is a second, weaker candidate (changes RMS-norm summation order, not matmul, and isn't obviously coopmat-gated).
+    Neither was reverted, and no fleet-impact bisection beyond this was run.
+  - **Why this was reported rather than patched:** this reads as the *same* category this section already documents
+    above for SSM_CONV_SPLIT/qwen3-coder -- near-tied logit margins tipped by batch-size-dependent GPU matmul
+    numerics (plain decode is M=1, speculative verify is M>1, and different M routes through different
+    Vulkan/coopmat kernel variants) -- not a new logic bug in the grammar engine or in the fork's drafting path.
+    `8e5a58df8`'s own commit message describes fixing real fp16-overflow correctness bugs for production models
+    ("handle fp32 overflows through scaling", "handle overflows in copy-to-fp16 activations"); reverting it (or
+    disabling coopmat1) to chase a tie-flip in a tiny test model is not a safe minimal fix, and the production fleet
+    runs AMD UMA nodes only -- no NVIDIA in production, so this has no known fleet impact and was deliberately left
+    unmitigated rather than traded against that upstream fix. The AMD/coopmat path was not available to test here.
+    Confirmed not fixed upstream as of this sync: only 4 commits exist between `202c1a229` and `upstream/master`
+    (`582eab718`, `7c2653acc`, `7592b61d3`, `cd4ed902e`), none touching `src/llama-grammar.cpp`,
+    `ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/`, or `src/llama-graph.cpp`.
+
